Subject: Compiled code can identify Array.prototype.push and pop

What this does
  - `JSAotGenLayout` gains the prototype tag of a builtin that takes a magic number.
  - `qjs_aot_array_builtin_fn` returns the function pointer of `js_array_push` or `js_array_pop`, which a
    C function object holds, with magic 0, when it is Array.prototype.push or pop.

Why we need it
  `a.push(x)` and `a.pop()` on a dense array were a call into the engine each: the call helper, the
  builtin's own checks and the length update, about 100 and 200 cycles. A generated site now tests that
  the callee is the builtin (class, prototype tag, magic and function pointer), that the receiver is a
  plain dense array (the initial array shape, extensible, standard array prototype, `length` an int equal
  to the count) and, for push, that the storage has room, and for pop, that the last element is not a
  hole: then the element is stored or taken and the count and `length` updated in place. Every other
  case, a full array included, is the call as before.

